Problem Statement: Predicting Customer Purchase Behavior

This problem can be approached by:

1. Regression

Objective:

Predict how much money a customer will spend.

Example: If a customer has high income, visits the website often, and responded to campaigns,
the model should predict a higher purchase amount.

Target :PurchaseAmount

Input Features :Age, Gender, AnnualIncome, WebsiteVisits,
TimeOnApp, PreviousPurchases, CampaignResponse, LoyaltyPoints, PreferredDevice, Region.

Algorithm used:

Linear Regression → simple, easy to understand.

2. Classification

Objective:

Predict whether a customer will make a purchase (Yes/No).

Example: If a customer has low visits and no campaign response, the model should predict No Purchase.

Target:PurchaseDecision (Yes or No).

Input Features:Age, Gender, AnnualIncome, WebsiteVisits,
TimeOnApp, PreviousPurchases, CampaignResponse, LoyaltyPoints, PreferredDevice, Region

Algorithm used

i)Logistic Regression → simple, good starting point.

ii)Decision Tree Classifier

The Decision Tree learns rules from customer information (like age, income, and previous purchases)
to decide if a customer is likely to buy.

I also applied hyperparameter tuning (changing tree depth, minimum samples, etc.) to improve accuracy.
